<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- RUT_Ported_GravForge.xml - RESEARCH_TRIO_RETIRE_1. The one "supporting def"
     the owner's ruling named explicitly ("plus whatever supporting defs they
     reference, e.g. GravForge's building"). als.gravtech's Grav Forge is the
     hub of the whole GravForge/GravTuning/GravBionics/GravWeapon/AdvShipParts/
     BlackHole_GT/GTbc_BigCannons research cluster - without it, GravForge (the
     research) unlocks nothing to build. Ported here, same defName/recipe
     defNames, from workshop 3545374124 1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/GravForge_GT.xml,
     read directly off disk this session (never from memory).

     Also ports the three GravForge-exclusive items its own recipes and
     killedLeavings reference (checked against the live def dump and vanilla
     Data/ before deciding each needed a port):
       - Gravitonium        (ThingDefs_Items/Gravitonium_GT.xml)   - GravForge's
         own recipe product, techLevel Ultra armor/insulation stuff.
       - ChunkSlagPlasteel_GT (ThingDefs_Misc/ChunkSlag_GT.xml)    - the
         building's killedLeavings chunk; <smeltable> lets vanilla's own
         Smelter mechanic recover Plasteel from it with no extra recipe.
       - UnfinishedGravcore  (ThingDefs_Items/Unfinished_GT.xml)   - the
         Make_GravcoreGF recipe's unfinishedThingDef.
     Gravcore and GravlitePanel (referenced throughout) are NOT ported - both
     are vanilla Odyssey DLC items (Data/Odyssey/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/
     Items_Resource_Misc.xml), confirmed absent from every als.gravtech file.
     UnfinishedComponent is vanilla Core, same reasoning.

     NOT PORTED, explicitly out of scope this pass (see this item's ledger
     note / RESEARCH_TRIO_RETIRE_1.md for the full list): GravWeapon's four
     personal weapons (GravCannon_GT/GravBlaster_GT/GravgunRifle_GT/
     GravHammer_GT + Apparel_GravPack_GT/Apparel_GravBelts_GT), GravBionics'
     implants (GravBionic_GT.xml), GravTuning's AI-core copy recipe target
     (kept below since it lives on GravForge itself), AdvShip_* ship parts
     (7 buildings), and als.gravtech.bc's whole "big cannons" building family
     (9 buildings). Those research nodes exist and are correctly costed/
     tabbed/prereq'd after this port, but currently unlock no new content of
     their own - a real, scoped, named follow-on (not invented or guessed at
     here).

     Textures copied verbatim from the same donor:
       Textures/Building/GravForge/GravForge_{east,north,south}.png
       Textures/Item/Gravitonium.png
       Textures/Unfinished/UnfinishedGravcore.png
     (west is engine-mirrored from east, same as the donor shipped it -
     drawRotated is false and only 3 rotations were ever provided).
-->
<Defs>

